it's business as usual for these  fishermen in the Thai province of punga  but on this day 15 years ago a tsunami  triggered by a magnitude nine point one  earthquake devastated the coastline here  waves as high as seventeen and a half  meters came crashing in from the ocean  killing nearly 5,000 people in this  village alone with half the population  wiped out nearly everyone who has lost a  relative or even a friend nowand  chantara Wong knows too well that no  matter how many years have passed the  pain of losing your children never goes  away  I don't think they died on the day the  tsunami hit we couldn't find them until  the 28th and their bodies hadn't  decomposed at all I often imagine how  much they would have thought about me  before they took their last breaths but  we couldn't find them we couldn't help  them this is stuck with me and every  time I think about it it hurts  these images shocked the world the day  after Christmas  shortly before 8 a.m. in 2004 the  earthquake struck under the sea in  northern Indonesia it rippled across the  Indian Ocean triggering a tsunami that  hit dozens of countries in Asia and  along Africa's East Coast getting close  to 230,000 people and it happened during  peak tourist season the majority of  those who died were in Indonesia entire  villages were flattened and the carnage  of that day is still fresh on the minds  of those living in at Chopra vents the  worst hit area where a hundred and  seventy thousand people were killed on  behalf of the government and people of  akshay today we formally want to thank  more than a hundred and fifty countries  that have been involved in helping  rehabilitation and reconstruction no one  knew the tsunami was coming on that day  there was no early warning systems in  place but it was a global lesson learned  [Music]  since then more than four hundred  million dollars has been spent across 28  countries on detectors survivors say the  technology is not enough though and that  public awareness and education are  necessary to save people's lives  Zaara hayaat al-jazeera
 

